CAT = "s24Financial"; SEG = "FIN"
Q = [
('Under SEC Rule 15c3-1, a broker-dealer that uses the alternative standard must keep net capital of at least the greater of $250,000 or:',
 '2% of aggregate debit items', ['5% of total assets', '10% of customer credits', '1,500% of aggregate indebtedness'],
 'Rule 15c3-1(a)(1)(ii) sets the alternative standard minimum at the greater of $250,000 or 2 percent of aggregate debit items computed under the reserve formula.'),
('An introducing firm receives customer securities but promptly forwards them to its clearing firm and holds no customer funds. Its minimum net capital is:',
 '$50,000', ['$5,000', '$100,000', '$250,000'],
 'Rule 15c3-1(a)(2)(iv) sets a $50,000 minimum for a broker-dealer that introduces customer accounts on a fully disclosed basis and receives but does not hold customer securities.'),
('An introducing firm that never receives customer funds or securities, sending all checks straight to its clearing firm, needs minimum net capital of:',
 '$5,000', ['$50,000', '$100,000', '$250,000'],
 'Rule 15c3-1(a)(2)(vi) sets a $5,000 minimum for a broker or dealer that does not receive, directly or indirectly, or hold funds or securities for customers and does not carry customer accounts.'),
("A broker-dealer's net capital falls below its required minimum. Under SEC Rule 17a-11 it must give notice:",
 'That same day', ['Within 24 hours', 'Within five business days', 'With its next FOCUS report'],
 "Rule 17a-11(a) requires notice the same day when net capital is below the minimum required by Rule 15c3-1, specifying the firm's net capital requirement and its current amount."),
("A firm's total net capital drops to 115% of its required minimum. Under SEC Rule 17a-11 it must:",
 'Send an early warning notice within 24 hours', ['Stop doing all securities business that same day', 'File only with its next FOCUS report', 'Do nothing until it falls below 100%'],
 'Rule 17a-11(b) requires notice within 24 hours when net capital is less than 120 percent of the required minimum. This early warning level comes before an actual deficiency.'),
('A broker-dealer on the aggregate indebtedness standard finds that its aggregate indebtedness is 1,300% of its net capital. It must:',
 'Notify its regulators within 24 hours', ['Close every customer account at once', 'Wait until the ratio reaches 1,500% before acting', "Report it at the firm's next annual audit"],
 "Rule 17a-11(b)(1) treats aggregate indebtedness above 1,200 percent of net capital as an early warning level requiring notice within 24 hours. The rule's ceiling is 1,500 percent."),
('Without first notifying the SEC and FINRA, a carrying firm may not withdraw equity capital that, net, exceeds in any 30 calendar days:',
 '30% of its excess net capital', ['10% of its total assets', '50% of its excess net capital', '5% of its aggregate debit items'],
 'Rule 15c3-1(e)(1)(i) requires written notice two business days before withdrawals, advances or loans that on a net basis exceed 30 percent of excess net capital in any 30 calendar day period.'),
('Under SEC Rule 15c3-3, when the reserve formula shows customer credits exceed customer debits, the firm must:',
 'Deposit the difference in a special reserve account', ['Pay the excess to customers as interest on their balances', 'Lend the excess to its clearing firm overnight', 'Keep the excess as part of its net capital'],
 'Rule 15c3-3(e) requires a carrying firm to keep in a Special Reserve Bank Account for the Exclusive Benefit of Customers an amount at least equal to the excess of credits over debits in the reserve formula.'),
("Under SEC Rule 15c3-3, a carrying firm must keep customers' fully paid and excess margin securities:",
 'In its physical possession or control', ['Pledged to a bank for firm loans', 'Lent out to other broker-dealers', "Registered in the representative's name"],
 'Rule 15c3-3(b) requires prompt possession or control of all fully paid and excess margin securities carried for customers, so they cannot be used to finance the firm.'),
('Under FINRA Rule 4560, members report short interest positions in equity securities:',
 'Twice a month', ['Once a quarter', 'Every trading day', 'Once a year'],
 'Rule 4560 requires members to report gross short positions in all customer and proprietary accounts twice a month, as of designated settlement dates FINRA publishes.'),
('Before an introducing firm and a clearing firm start operating under a carrying agreement, Rule 4311 requires:',
 'FINRA to review and approve the agreement', ['Each customer to sign a copy of the agreement', 'The SEC to register the agreement', 'A state regulator to approve the clearing fees'],
 'Rule 4311(a) requires carrying agreements to be submitted to and approved by FINRA before use; customers are told in writing at account opening which firm carries their account and what it does.'),
('Under SEC Rule 10b-16, a firm that extends credit in margin accounts must disclose the terms of that credit:',
 'At account opening and at least quarterly', ['Only when a margin call is issued to the customer', 'Once, when the account is first funded', 'Only if the customer asks for it in writing'],
 'Rule 10b-16 requires written disclosure of the interest rate and how interest is computed at account opening, plus periodic statements at least quarterly showing the balance and interest charged.'),
]
